WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.630
Detective Dan's dedicated episode in Season
5B is a riot of crazy misadventures crammed

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:10.370
full of easter eggs to previous episodes over
the entire series.

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:15.099
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and today
we're dedicating this video to Daniel Espinoza

00:00:15.099 --> 00:00:20.109
and all the insane details hidden in his Naked
and Afraid episode, plus some intriguing theories

00:00:20.109 --> 00:00:24.500
for his return in Season 6.
Spoilers, of course, so take care.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:28.580
Check out the walls at Dan's home and you'll
see several posters for Weaponizer, one of

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:32.079
his and Lucifer's favourite action movie franchises,
"Personal fave:

00:00:32.079 --> 00:00:35.629
Weaponizer 4: The Last Arsenal."
"So good."

00:00:35.629 --> 00:00:39.670
which in the alternate universe of Season
3's Once Upon A Time episode actually starred

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:43.610
Chloe as a thief-turned-cop.
And there's a bunch of very funny horror movie

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:47.160
posters too.
Bog Shark has the tagline "The water turns

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:52.230
red this winter!" and stars Joe Mason who
works in the Lucifer art department as a graphic

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:55.230
designer.
The Zamboni goes with the tagline

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.070
"He'll put you on ice...
permanently",

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:02.640
a hat-tip to the first Deadpool movie.
"You're about to be killed by a zamboni.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.111
In five minutes!"
The Plunge is a call-back to Season 3 where

00:01:06.111 --> 00:01:09.630
its producer was using her movies to launder
money for a drug cartel.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.620
"Alexa made The Plunge?
A group of teens, they have to travel to the

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.240
center of the Earth to unclog this blocked-up
magma.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.791
Oh, man."
And there's also a poster for Return of the

00:01:16.791 --> 00:01:20.970
Leechmen, which tells us this sequel is "even
suckier"!

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.640
One of cinema's Biggest Bads of all time gets
a shout out when Dan reveals that Luci's mind

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:30.650
games just don't have the same effect on him
now he knows he's dealing with the actual

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:32.640
devil:
"It's like being teased by Genghis Khan or

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.720
Darth Vader."
Dan comparing Luci to the Star Wars villain

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:40.270
makes me think back to the scene in Season
1 when Lucifer picked up a voice modulator

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:43.800
at a crime scene and did this:
"Detective, I am your father."

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.520
Which is even more amusing in the context
of Season 5B because now Lucifer is God, he

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.510
kind of is everyone's father!
Of course, it's one thing to jokingly do a

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:57.370
Vader voice yourself and quite another being
likened to the Dark Side by someone else;

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:00.850
so, Lucifer is not happy!
"I'm not some bloody villain, Daniel."

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:05.800
Of course, Luci's reaction was to be expected;
after all, since the very first season, time

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.560
and again, he's told anyone who'll listen
that he gets an undeservedly bad rap:

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:14.190
"'Oh, the Devil made me do it.'
I have never made any one of them do anything."

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:18.410
By the way, Lucifer already knows he's going
to make Dan pay for his wicked words at the

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:21.580
top of episode 12:
"Don't come to me begging for any favours."

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.030
"Don't worry, I won't."
... because it's all a set-up.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:27.510
Cue Dan asking for that favour 15 minutes
later in the episode!

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.390
"Lucifer, I need a favour.

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.200
Waking up naked in unexpected places and situations
is something that's happened to Dan before.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:38.630
Back in Season 1, he woke up nude in Chloe's
bed, after Maze knocked him out and left him

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:42.610
there to try and force him back with his ex
so that Lucifer wouldn't be interested in

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:43.860
her any more.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.910
This episode isn't Dan's first run-in with
Los X.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:51.670
Back in Season 4, he and Maze came to blows
with the gang after turning up at their headquarters

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:56.860
to try and find the killer of two former members.
In fact, Maze later tearfully recalls that

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:02.970
moment as a happy memory she has of Dan:
"When Dan and I pulverized that gang together.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:04.310
It was beautiful."

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:08.590
Curiously, this episode finds Dan going through
a number of events similar to ones experienced

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:13.290
by his ex, Chloe, previously in the series:
both have been poisoned and been in a race

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:17.200
against the clock to get the antidote, though,
obviously, Dan's was a prank;

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.930
On top of that, both detectives have also
been in car crashes where their vehicle was

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:24.790
T-boned, and both those collisions were deliberately
caused by celestials

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:29.620
– Lucifer in Dan's case, and Uriel in Chloe's.
Both Dan and Chloe have been kidnapped in

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:35.160
situations orchestrated by Michael, with Dan
being taken by mercenaries employed by Lucifer's

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.160
twin.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.550
Heads literally roll after an old cop friend
persuades Dan to take a package back to LA

00:03:40.550 --> 00:03:44.350
during a prisoner transfer.
And there was a hint at what was to come after

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:49.010
he agreed to do the favour when Brad Pitt's
famous line "What's in the box?"

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:52.310
from the end of Se7en made an appearance during
Dan's journey home:

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:55.720
"What's in the box?"
Oh, and this isn't the first time that Dan's

00:03:55.720 --> 00:04:00.330
had to deal with a head in a box either, as
in Season 2 a mystery package turned up for

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:04.950
him at the precinct, and inside was the head
of Russian mobster Boris Sokolov, who'd been

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:08.670
about to testify against the real killer of
Chloe's father.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:13.140
When Dan's old improv crew rock up out of
nowhere, it's a hint that Lucifer's behind

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:17.639
all this as he's known about them since he
decided to shadow Dan in Season 2.

00:04:17.639 --> 00:04:22.370
"We haven't seen you in improv in ages."
"I've been pretty busy lately."

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:26.900
It's true Dan's had a lot to deal with of
late, but he also told Amenadiel in Season

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:29.380
4,
"I'm not really that into improv anymore".

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:33.779
When Dan asks Lucifer to help him find a prisoner
who escaped while he was transporting her,

00:04:33.779 --> 00:04:38.330
it reminds Luci of one of their previous escapades:
"The last time you lost a fugitive.

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.469
12-year-old girl?
You soiling yourself on that roller coaster?

00:04:40.469 --> 00:04:42.960
"
"I didn't soil myself, Lucifer."

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:47.319
That's a throwback to Season 3 when a young
kid ran away to an amusement park while Dan

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:52.289
was taking her to the precinct and Lucifer
found the whole affair so funny that he had

00:04:52.289 --> 00:04:55.240
200 T-shirts made to remember it!

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:59.990
Another person Dan turns to for help is Ella,
who he asks for advice on the perfect murder:

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:02.690
"I actually do know how to fake the perfect
murder.

00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:06.150
Because...
I've been working on it for my novel.

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:08.979
It's about a forensic scientist who talks
to ghosts."

00:05:08.979 --> 00:05:13.639
This moment harks back to Season 3 where Ella
told Lucifer she was writing a book on that

00:05:13.639 --> 00:05:17.210
exact same subject.
Of course, the book is inspired by Ella's

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:20.460
own life:
"She's super cheerful, but really tortured.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:24.919
Totally transparent, but full of secrets."
As for the book's ghost character, that goes

00:05:24.919 --> 00:05:29.289
back to the bonus episode Boo Normal where
we learned that as a child Ella met what she

00:05:29.289 --> 00:05:34.699
thought was a ghost called Rae-Rae, but who
was actually Lucifer's angelic sister Azrael.

00:05:34.699 --> 00:05:39.520
Things get a bit awkward when Dan gets a lift
from Amenadiel, who's understandably not keen

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:42.330
on being treated like an Uber, or should that
be Uberdiel?

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:46.199
"Do I sort of climb on?
Okay.

00:05:46.199 --> 00:05:49.379
Oh!"
And when Dan warns Amenadiel that:

00:05:49.379 --> 00:05:53.270
"I may pass out."
it's a call-back to 5A's midseason finale

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:57.909
when Dan told Lucifer he was flown somewhere
by Michael, but doesn't know where because:

00:05:57.909 --> 00:06:01.449
"I kind of passed out on the flight there."
Oh man, I'm afraid of heights.

00:06:01.449 --> 00:06:03.099
You know what roller coasters do to me."

00:06:03.099 --> 00:06:07.581
When Dan doesn't want to get Maze involved
in the whole Luis and Los X situation, she

00:06:07.581 --> 00:06:11.430
reassures him that he can tell her anything:
"We killed a guy together."

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:15.690
"For the last time, we didn't kill a guy.
We made sure some dangerous people found him."

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:18.880
"Yeah, yeah, blah-blah-blah."
This is a long-running sort of joke in the

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:23.169
series as Maze has gleefully brought this
up on a number of occasions much to Dan's

00:06:23.169 --> 00:06:25.610
chagrin:
"I thought that we could, uh, celebrate our

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.499
righteous kill."
"We didn't kill anyone, okay?

00:06:27.499 --> 00:06:31.870
We gave karmic justice a little nudge."
And Maze's comment about their plan to deal

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.309
with Luis,
"Duh, we've done this before."

00:06:34.309 --> 00:06:39.220
is a nod back to Season 2 where she first
used her "Russian contacts" to help Dan deal

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:43.610
with another situation outside the law: making
the man who had Chloe's father killed pay

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:48.990
for that crime as he'd gotten away with it.
By the way, I think Dan's sensitivity to Maze's

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:52.999
comments that they killed a guy together indicates
some lingering guilt in the back of his mind

00:06:52.999 --> 00:06:56.800
and is one of the reasons his guilt takes
him to Hell at the end of the season.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:06:57.810
More on that later.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:03.430
If Dan was ever in any doubt about his innate
cop-ness, Maze sets him straight when she

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:06.749
informs him she's telling her Russian contacts
he's called Joe Stone:

00:07:06.749 --> 00:07:10.830
"Because Dan Espinoza sounds like a cop.
Joe Stone sounds cool.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.110
You need to be...
cool with these people."

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:18.080
And Maze isn't the only one to have recognised
Dan's unmistakeable law enforcement vibe:

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.809
"We're undercover, okay?"
"As if you could look like anything other

00:07:20.809 --> 00:07:23.099
than a cop."
"I do not look like a cop!"

00:07:23.099 --> 00:07:24.099
"Cop."

00:07:24.099 --> 00:07:28.520
The culmination of Dan's increasingly crazy
adventures has major Indiana Jones and The

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:32.300
Temple of Doom vibes:
from the nightclub setting to the shady deals

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:36.869
going down that lead to a big shoot-out, to
a woman being held as a bargaining chip,

00:07:36.869 --> 00:07:41.169
to both our protagonists having been poisoned
and scrabbling around on the floor for a vial

00:07:41.169 --> 00:07:46.020
of antidote that gets kicked out of reach.
Both sequences also have a period feel, with

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:51.080
Temple of Doom set in the mid-30s and featuring
Cole Porter's appropriately themed Anything

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:53.999
Goes;
while Dan's crew are decked out in old-timey

00:07:53.999 --> 00:07:59.780
costumes as 50s hit Vaya con Dios plays, a
fitting song title given all the dead bodies

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:03.619
by the end.
Plus, Dan may not be wearing a tux like Indy,

00:08:03.619 --> 00:08:08.849
but Lucifer does make him get dressed up and
notice how the double-meaning of Luci's words

00:08:08.849 --> 00:08:11.949
here devilishly reveals the whole thing is
just make-believe:

00:08:11.949 --> 00:08:16.330
"There won't be any actual violence, it's
all about appearances, hence why I insisted

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:17.619
on the suit."

00:08:17.619 --> 00:08:22.520
After all is revealed and the wrap party begins,
a pyramid of puddings is wheeled out to celebrate.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:27.589
A lovely touch given how much we know Dan
loves his puddings and perhaps it makes up

00:08:27.589 --> 00:08:30.499
for all the ones Lucifer's stolen off him
over the years.

00:08:30.499 --> 00:08:34.769
"My pudding, clearly labeled 'Dan', it's gone.
I'm just saying that a man's snacks, they're

00:08:34.769 --> 00:08:35.769
sacred, okay?"

00:08:35.769 --> 00:08:39.320
And even the dog that attacked Dan at the
bike shop is there at the bar, getting his

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:43.660
rewards for playing his part in the prank
like the very good boy that he is!

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:48.770
So, quite few things we see happen to Dan
in this episode are found on Lucifer's Operation

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:54.769
Payback board from the midseason finale, including
"severed head in a box", "send him to Tijuana",

00:08:54.769 --> 00:08:59.670
"hates dogs", and car crash.
And, as I mentioned earlier, Luci also delights

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:03.940
in reminding Dan of his previous terrible
experience with rollercoasters.

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:08.100
And although Dan doesn't believe he can fly
himself, he does hitch a ride through the

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.890
skies with Amenadiel.
"Why did you do all this?"

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:15.130
"Because you f- shot me Daniel."
And while Luci's not responsible for this,

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:18.920
"Convince him he's going to Hell" is something
that happens to Dan in the musical episode

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:23.070
after he meets Lucifer's father and realises
he slept with God's wife.

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:25.100
"Which means I'm definitely going to Hell."

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:29.600
Now, Dan's near-brush with death in his Naked
and Afraid episode turns out to be a gigantic

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:33.279
ruse by Lucifer
"Five million, four thousand, one hundred

00:09:33.279 --> 00:09:36.680
and fifty-seven dollars spent.
Totally worth it.!

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:41.110
but sadly Dan does die when he's shot in the
back by a merc in the season's penultimate

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:44.670
episode.
Dan's killer is played by guest star Rob Benedict,

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:49.860
who fans of the TV series Supernatural will
recognise as he played God on that show.

00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:53.941
It's ironic that after being exploded and
put back together by this show's God, and

00:09:53.941 --> 00:09:57.540
expecting him to finish the job at any moment:
"So, smite me.

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:00.630
Let's just get it over with."
in the end Dan does get killed but it's by

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:04.920
a God from another show.
And it was just heart-breaking when Trixie

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:08.980
discovered her dad was gone, and like her
mother Chloe, she too now has lost her father

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:10.130
in the line of duty.

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:15.690
And it seems especially cruel that despite
Dan's significant efforts at reform and self-improvement,

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:19.850
we discover from Amenadiel that Dan didn't
make it into Heaven, meaning any feelings

00:10:19.850 --> 00:10:24.290
of guilt he still had have taken him to Hell.
So, what could those things be?

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:28.180
Well, first of all, there's Charlotte whose
death Dan is still struggling to get over

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:32.080
in the first half of Season 5.
And Dan's feelings about her get even more

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:36.490
mixed up when he discovers she was the wife
of God, who in a vengeful, petty way decides

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:41.430
to explode Dan before quickly restoring him.
That moment literally puts the fear of God

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:45.829
into Dan and could well be something he'll
need to reconcile as part of his Hell Loop.

00:10:45.829 --> 00:10:50.310
Then there's his indirect involvement in the
Russian mob's murder of Perry Smith, the corrupt

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:54.120
prison warden who had Chloe's father assassinated,
as I mentioned earlier.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:58.160
Although obviously many would say Smith got
what he deserved, Dan may still be harbouring

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:02.089
some guilt over his own involvement.
And, of course, there's also Dan's sketchy

00:11:02.089 --> 00:11:06.759
history and association with the Palmetto
case from Season 1, which gets a mention in

00:11:06.759 --> 00:11:08.640
episode 12.
"Couple years back, I got into some trouble

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.810
on Palmetto Street.
And I&nbsp;realized that when your motives are

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:15.240
bad and when you're only out for yourself,
your actions have consequences."

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:19.079
The good news is that Luci's encounter with
Mr Said-Out Bitch in Heaven proves that it

00:11:19.079 --> 00:11:22.560
is possible for someone to escape their own
personal Hell Loop.

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:24.860
"I faced my family.
My guilt."

00:11:24.860 --> 00:11:29.139
Despite his chequered history, Dan has demonstrated
incredible resilience and strength in some

00:11:29.139 --> 00:11:33.170
especially extreme situations, from the time
he wielded Azrael's Blade:

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:36.470
"You're fighting the blade.
Which indicates a strength I didn't know you

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:38.620
had."
...to his perseverance during the Naked and

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:42.810
Afraid episode, which Luci recognised via
the backhanded compliment he gave him at the

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:44.740
end of the huge prank.
"At every opportunity to quit, I knew that

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:49.110
your oafish optimism would keep you going.
I suppose I realized that whenever you're

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:54.200
given a choice, you always at least try and
do the right thing."

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:58.730
An intriguing theory as to what we could see
for Dan in Season 6 was posted by Kevin Allen

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:03.190
on my ending explained video, which says that
Dan will get an episode all to himself,

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:07.310
"where he needs to solve a case in his Hell
Loop with Lucifer, Amenadiel, Maze, and others

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:10.930
popping in to try and help him.
He will eventually solve the case (which will

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:15.290
mirror his own life and his mistakes) and
reunite with Charlotte in Heaven."

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:19.410
Something I can see that could also get added
into the mix is now that Lucifer is God, he'll

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:22.519
try to reform the way that Heaven and Hell
are run.

00:12:22.519 --> 00:12:26.410
Remember that Luci was particularly angry
at the unfairness of Dan's death and how he'd

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:29.579
ended up in Hell.
"The system is not only broken.

00:12:29.579 --> 00:12:32.180
It's unjust.
I wanted to be God for the wrong reasons,

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:37.600
but now, I no longer want to be God.
I have to be God."

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:42.480
That line about the system being broken and
unjust is giving me vibes of The Good Place,

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:44.850
which there was actually an easter egg to
in the finale.

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:49.410
And Luci's words in this speech might hint
at an alternate resolution for how Dan can

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:54.270
get out of Hell, although actor Kevin Alejandro
has implied that what's important is that

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:58.160
Dan does this by himself.
So, while he may get advice from others, as

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:03.069
Mr Said Out Bitch did, ultimately, Dan will
have to put that advice into practice himself,

00:13:03.069 --> 00:13:07.610
just as Mr S.O.B did and just as Chloe did
too when she forgave herself for Dan's death

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:08.610
in the finale.

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:12.959
And I'll be talking more Season 6 theories
in my next Lucifer video, which I'll add a

00:13:12.959 --> 00:13:16.300
link to here and in the video description
as soon as it's ready.

00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:19.680
Now, how do you think Dan will get out of
Hell in Season 6?

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:23.769
And what were your favourite Dan moments from
his episode or the series as a whole?

00:13:23.769 --> 00:13:28.399
Let me know in the comments below.
Tap left to discover the top 50 easter eggs

00:13:28.399 --> 00:13:34.110
in Season 5 or tap right for a full explanation
of how Lucifer survived his journey to Heaven.

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:37.129
And if you enjoyed this, a thumbs-up and a
share are hugely appreciated.

00:13:37.129 --> 00:13:40.889
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

